-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",356,{
[11361]="70051F7C\n1\tDaily Reward -- Tier 1\tYou have returned to the high cliffs above Helegrod to face Storvâgûn.\n",
[11362]="70051F7E\n1\tDaily Reward -- Tier 2 (Cap Level)\tYou have returned to the high cliffs above Helegrod to face Storvâgûn.\n",
[11363]="70066759\n1\tComplete the mission: Call of the Sea\tSpeak with the stowaway and listen well to his tale. This is the beginning of his life at sea.\n2\tTalk to Falnavar\tSpeak with the stowaway and allow him to finish recounting the events of that night long ago.\n",
[11364]="70066761\n1\tComplete the mission: Attack on Pelargir\tThe mariner's tale continues with details of an assault on the river-port town of Pelargir.\n2\tTalk to Falnavar\tThe mariner wishes to speak with you to provide the conclusion to this chapter.\n",
[11365]="70066760\n1\tComplete Mission: The Tolfalas Shore\tThe mariner's tale is to continue as he reminisces about the attack on the Corsairs they found at the shores of Tolfalas.\n2\tTalk to Falnavar\tKnowing now how the battle on the shore transpired, you should speak with the mariner.\n",
[11366]="7006675C\n1\tComplete Mission: My Bosom Friend\tThere is more still to the mariner's tale. He bids you listen to the story of how he and the captain became fast friends.\n2\tTalk to Falnavar\tAfter hearing how the captain and the mariner grew close it is time to speak with the mariner once again.\n",
[11367]="70066758\n1\tComplete Mission: The Nenglor\tThere is something more to the mariner's tale as his countenance falls grim.\n2\tTalk to Falnavar\tYou know the fate of that night and the incident that befell the captain and the mariner. Return to the mariner to hear more.\n",
[11368]="70066763\n1\tComplete Mission: The Nenglor Reborn\tAfter a harsh reprimand for the loss of their ship, the captain set about building the Nenglor anew.\n2\tTalk to Falnavar\tWith the Nenglor rebuilt, the mariner's tale seems to be taking a different turn.\n",
[11369]="7006675E\n1\tComplete Mission: The Sermon\tListen to the tale that the mariner tells, something clearly went amiss after the Nenglor was rebuilt.\n2\tTalk to Falnavar\tThe captain seemed to become unhinged, in a fashion. Return to the mariner now and hear their thoughts.\n",
[11370]="7006675B\n1\tComplete Mission: To Plot Revenge\tAnger in his voice, the mariner continue his tale. Listen further.\n2\tTalk to Falnavar\tYou understand the intent now of the raid, and the mariner will continue his tale.\n",
[11371]="70066762\n1\tComplete Mission: Marked\tThe tale continues with the pursuit of the Corsair seemingly drawing to an end.\n2\tTalk to Falnavar\tTragedy befell the mariner, but the tale feels strange, something in the telling is... inconsistent.\n",
[11372]="7006675A\n1\tComplete Mission: The Beast\tA slip of the tongue? It is unclear, but the mariner's tale continues on.\n2\tTalk to Falnavar\tThe beast is defeated, but a mystery is revealed. Return to the mariner and tell him what you discovered.\n",
[11373]="7006675F\n1\tComplete Mission: A Final Vengeance\tThe last request? Perhaps. Speak with the mariner to go to the place where Yarikh is, and defeat the Corsair villain, once and for all.\n2\tSpeak with Falnavar\tReturn to the mariner and speak with him to inform him that the deed is complete.\n3\tRead the note you collected from Falnavar\tFalnavar's death is tragic, but there is a final note that he provided you.\n",
[11374]="70066757\n1\tSpeak with the man\tThe old man is injured gravely and it seems that there is no hope to close his wounds. His request is simple, stay and listen to his tale so that he is not forgotten. Will you see this through?\n2\tSpeak with Falnavar\tFalnavar paused, but it seems there is more he has to say. Ask him to continue.\n3\tSpeak with Falnavar\tFalnavar paused again. Perhaps you should see if there is more that he wishes to tell you.\n4\tContinue speaking with Falnavar\tContinue listening to Falnavar's tale.\n",
[11375]="700660D0\n1\tDefeat Orcs (total: 12)\tTharnion is concerned about the growing number of Orcs who have started to gather west of the city of Calembel. You should defeat Orcs at Roz Ladâr, their camp in western Lamedon.\n2\tReturn to Tharnion\tYou should let Tharnion know that you greatly lessened the Orc population at Roz Ladâr. Tharnion is in Calembel.\n",
[11376]="70065669\n1\tGo to Lord Sirgon's manor\tNasar has asked you to bring up the Corsairs' predicament with Lord Sirgon. Sirgon's manor is located in the north-west corner of East Pelargir.\n2\tTalk to the guard in the courtyard\tA guard has gestured for you to stop. You should talk to him outside Sirgon's East Pelargir manor.\n3\tTalk to Celebros\tCelebros seems interested in hearing what you have to say. You should talk to her about Nasar's request outside Sirgon's East Pelargir manor.\n",
[11377]="70041C80\n1\tRecover buried pillage near the marooned ship (total: 6)\tThe marooned ship and its crew can be found to the south-west of Aerthir upon the Anduin. A rowing boat on the shore will allow for swifter passage. Aerin has asked you to help recover pillage from the Corsairs that have become trapped on shoals in the Anduin.\n2\tDeliver the pillage to Aerin at Aerthir\tAerin can be found in the lighthouse at Aerthir in southern-central Lebennin. You have recovered a great deal of pillage from the marooned Corsairs and should now bring it to Aerin.\n",
[11378]="7003707C\n1\tDefeat Strangbera\tSomewhere in the Roaring Hills roams a large and dangerous bear. You should find and defeat the great bear Strangbera.\n2\tDefeat Strangbera\tSomewhere in the Roaring Hills roams a large and dangerous bear. You should find and defeat the great bear Strangbera.\n3\tComplete\tThe dangerous bear that once roamed the Roaring Hills is no more.\n",
[11379]="70028C95\n1\tRecover strange weapons (total: 3)\tThe strange weapons Answith spoke of may be found on the Dunlendings who dwell at Brôntrig. Answith has asked you to recover the strange weapons from the Dunlendings at Brôntrig.\n2\tBring the strange weapons to Answith in the Isendale\tAnswith is encamped near the tower west of Brôntrig. You should bring the weapons you recovered to Answith.\n",
[11380]="70058C92\n1\tScout Caivád Sâr\tCaivád Sâr can be found in the northern reaches of Elderslade in the War of Three Peaks. Agnar Brokentooth has ordered you to aid Múta in assessing and eliminating the danger posed by Dourhands who recently arrived at Caivád Sâr.\n2\tFind Múta in Tûr Ágal\tMúta can be found somewhere within Tûr Ágal, the tower in the centre of Caivád Sâr. You have scouted Caivád Sâr and should now find and aid Múta in Tûr Ágal.\n3\tTalk to Múta in Tûr Ágal\tMúta can be found beside the staircase to the right of the entrance of Tûr Ágal, the tower in the centre of Caivád Sâr. You have found Múta in Tûr Ágal. You should talk to her and learn what is to be done.\n4\tAid Múta with 'Disloyal to the Crown'\030Aid Múta with 'Servants of War'\tMúta can be found beside the staircase to the right of the entrance of Tûr Ágal, the tower in the centre of Caivád Sâr. Múta has asked you to aid her in Tûr Ágal.\n5\tTalk to Múta in Tûr Ágal\tMúta can be found beside the staircase to the right of the entrance of Tûr Ágal, the tower in the centre of Caivád Sâr. You have aided Múta in assessing the danger posed by the Dourhands and freed Longbeards captured and held at at Caivád Sâr. You should report back to Múta.\n",
[11381]="7001AB98\n1\tCollect strange ash (total: 6)\tSâd-en-Dagor is in Dol Guldur, north-east of Helethir. Stirnir has asked you to enter Sâd-en-Dagor and recover the strange ash from the Black Númenórean sorcerers there.\n",
[11382]="70008357\n1\tDefeat hill-beasts (total: 10)\tHill-beasts stalk the slopes of Nád Nathair to the north-west of Tasgall's camp-site, in Fasach-larran. Tasgall has asked you to defeat many hill-beasts while he thinks of some way to resist them more effectively.\n2\tTalk to Tasgall\tTasgall's camp-site is north of Aughaire and south-east of Nád Nathair. You have defeated many hill-beasts and should now return to Tasgall.\n",
[11383]="70046C48\n1\tTalk to Anborn in Henneth Annûn\tAnborn can be found in Henneth Annûn. Mablung has asked you to speak to Anborn about the strange travellers that passed through Ithilien before the battle brought them to Osgiliath.\n",
[11384]="700190FD\n1\tReturn to Hasta\030Collect evidence of strange creatures (total: 10)\tThe creatures under suspicion are rumoured to be found to the south and west of the Rotting Cellar. Hasta has asked you to confirm the reports of strange creatures in the Water-works by bringing back sufficient evidence of their existence.\n",
[11385]="7001ABA2\n1\tCollect meat-scraps (total: 6)\tDraugdegil lies to the north of Helethir, just inside the gate of Fennas Guldur.\n",
[11386]="7002FD0D\n1\tSee what can be seen in the depths of the Ent's gaze\tThe sleepy Ent is along the faint path at the southern edge of Fangorn Forest. You should speak with Ashlimb.\n2\tTalk to Ashlimb\tThe sleepy Ent is along the faint path at the southern edge of Fangorn Forest. You should speak with Ashlimb.\n",
[11387]="70065B4B\n1\tDiscover the camp of the Ruins of Ethillorn\tThe Ruins of Ethillorn have become host to the Ruthless Dead. Reach the Ruins of Ethillorn, south of Linhir.\n2\tDestroy corrupted relics (total: 6)\tStrange items within the ruins of Ethillorn have become possessed of an unseemly power. Destroy corrupted relics in the Ruins of Ethillorn, south of Linhir.\n3\tYou have destroyed many relics.\t\n",
[11388]="70034011\n1\tSearch the strange spire to the north\tThe strange spires on the landscape can be found north, south, and south-west of the cross-roads in the south-eastern Whitshaws. You should scout the northern ice-spire at the lake's edge in the Whitshaws.\n2\tSearch the strange spire to the south\tThe strange spires on the landscape can be found north, south, and south-west of the cross-roads in the south-eastern Whitshaws. You should scout the southern-most spire of ice in the Whitshaws.\n3\tSearch the strange spire to the south-west of the cross-roads\tThe strange spires on the landscape can be found north, south, and south-west of the cross-roads in the south-eastern Whitshaws. You should scout the western-most ice-spire in the southern Whitshaws.\n4\tFind Cyneberg at Dunfast\tCyneberg has ridden ahead to Dunfast, which lies westward along the Whitshaws road from Forlaw. You should meet up with Cyneberg at Dunfast.\n",
[11389]="70028C9D\n1\tBring the sigil to Garrun in the Isendale\tGarrun is at his camp, north along the ridgeline. You should bring the sigil you found to Garrun.\n",
[11390]="700190FE\n1\tBring Hethuwen's notes to Hasta\030Return to Hasta with Hethuwen's notes\tHasta is at the Rotting Cellar in the Water-works, far to the west from the Shadowed Refuge. Hethuwen has given you a phial of the substance she uncovered during her experiment, along with copious notes. She has asked you to bring these to Hasta in the Water-works.\n",
[11391]="70052CE5\n1\tDefeat Gladden gloomwaters (total: 12)\tGladden gloomwaters can be found along the river Gladden. You should defeat Gladden gloomwaters.\n2\tCompleted\tDefeated many Gladden gloomwaters.\n",
[11392]="700300FA\n1\tFind out where the wounded man went\tThe Rohirrim limped off to the north-west, moving deeper into the Eaves of Fangorn. You should search for the injured Rohirrim.\n2\tExamine the bedroll more closely\tThe injured man's bedroll is at his camp-site, apparently abandoned. You should examing the bedroll to see if any other belongings were left behind.\n3\tCompleted\tThe abandoned camp-site is in the centre of Fangorn's eaves.\n",
})
